  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Women&#x2019;s Rights Programme in Nepal, implemented by ActionAid and local partners aims to contribute to resilient livlehoods for marginalised women and girls, including survivors of violence. The main objective is to improve the incomes and sustainability of livelihoods of marginalised women and survivors of violence by enhancing business skills, access to markets and participation in decision making.  Objective: Enhanced economic resilience of marginalized women and survivors with increased incomes and safer livelihood alternatives. Outcome: Marginalized women and girls, including survivors of violence, are enjoying resilient livelihood alternatives.</narrative>
  </description>
